# [[.Name]]

Generated from the bus-2.0 Go boilerplate with
`db=[[if .Both]]postgres,mongo[[else]][[.DB]][[end]] kafka=[[.Kafka]] redis=[[.Redis]]`.
[[- if .Both]]

Postgres is the primary database (entities, outbox, inbox). MongoDB is a
secondary database, reached with `Deps.Mongo(ctx)` in `internal/bootstrap`;
it connects only when first used.
[[- if .Kafka]] The sample `internal/store/activity` writes one Mongo
document per consumed item event.
[[- end]]
[[- end]]

## Run locally

```bash
make up                                   # postgres, mongo, kafka, redis (repo root)
cp services/[[.Name]]/.env.example services/[[.Name]]/.env
[[- if eq .DB "postgres"]]
make db svc=[[.Name]]                     # create the database
make migrate-diff svc=[[.Name]] name=init # first time only: generate SQL from the ent schema
make migrate-up svc=[[.Name]]
[[- end]]
[[- if .Kafka]]
make run svc=[[.Name]] mode=topics        # create Kafka topics
[[- end]]
make run svc=[[.Name]] mode=all           # API[[if and .Kafka .HasDB]] + outbox relay[[end]][[if .Kafka]] + consumer[[end]]
```

API on `http://localhost:[[.Port]]`, health/metrics on `http://localhost:[[.AdminPort]]`.
[[- if .HasDB]]

```bash
CID=0190a8f0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
curl -s -X POST localhost:[[.Port]]/v1/items \
  -H "X-Company-ID: $CID" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: $(uuidgen)" \
  -d '{"name":"Dhaka → Chattogram"}'
curl -s localhost:[[.Port]]/v1/items -H "X-Company-ID: $CID"
```
[[- end]]

## Run modes

| Mode | What it runs |
|---|---|
| `api` | public HTTP API on `HTTP_ADDR` |
[[- if and .Kafka .HasDB]]
| `relay` | outbox → Kafka publisher (leader-elected) |
[[- end]]
[[- if .Kafka]]
| `consumer` | Kafka consumer group `[[.Name]].item-events` |
| `topics` | create Kafka topics (local only) |
[[- end]]
| `all` | everything in one process (local only) |

## Layout

```
cmd/[[.Name]]/          main: config, run modes
internal/config/        env configuration
internal/bootstrap/     dependency wiring per run mode
internal/api/           HTTP handlers, permissions
[[- if .HasDB]]
internal/domain/        business types
internal/service/       business logic (+ unit tests with fakes)
internal/store/         persistence ([[.DB]][[if and .Both .Kafka]]; activity/ = Mongo sample[[end]])
[[- end]]
[[- if .Kafka]]
internal/events/        owned topics, event types, payloads
internal/consumer/      Kafka handlers
[[- end]]
[[- if eq .DB "postgres"]]
ent/schema/             ent schema (run `make gen` after changes)
migrations/             Atlas SQL migrations
[[- end]]
```

The `Item` entity is a sample. Replace it with your own entities and keep
the patterns: company scoping, outbox events, inbox claims, status
instead of delete, permission check per record.
